        "original_id": "80d6c226-d414-55cf-9ec1-7d768cdb7065",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Martin Flavin, Peter Benchley, George Archainbaud, Beulah Marie Dix\n- Works: Three Who Loved\n- Roles: playwright, novelist, author, screenwriter, director, screenwriter\n\nFacts:\n- Martin Archer Flavin was born on November 2, 1883, and he was an American playwright and novelist.\n- Three Who Loved was released in 1931 as an American Pre-Code drama film.\n- Three Who Loved was directed by George Archainbaud.\n- Three Who Loved was adapted from a screenplay by Beulah Marie Dix.\n- Three Who Loved was based on a story by Pulitzer Prize-winning author Martin Flavin.\n- Peter Bradford Benchley was born on May 8, 1940, and he was an American author and screenwriter.\n- Martin Archer Flavin died on December 27, 1967.\n- Peter Bradford Benchley died on February 11, 2006.",
